---
id: SCR-014   kind: screen   name: Pay for order
app: APP-002   module: MOD-003   screen_type: checkout   surface: phone
roles: [ROL-001, ROL-006, ROL-007, ROL-009]
tiers: {purpose: default, regions: default, actions: default, states: default}
provenance: ["compass:SCR-014", "model:spec.scrn", "user:FTR-003"]
stories: [US-S003]
---
purpose: Lets the buyer pay online for the selected order and review the amount including the delivery fee.
route: {name: pay_for_order, path: /pay_for_order, params: [], guard: [signed_in, role_has_access]}
reached_from: [SCR-013.open_pay_for_order]   leads_to: [SCR-015]
regions:   # alphabetical by key; the order carries no meaning
  - {key: amount_due_order, shape: key_values, what: what the user pays for and the amount due, bind: [ENT-006.produce_total, ENT-006.delivery_fee], importance: primary}
  - {key: amount_due_payment, shape: key_values, what: what the user pays for and the amount due, bind: [ENT-007.amount], importance: primary}
  - {key: methods_payment, shape: options, what: the ways the user can pay, bind: [OP-S028], importance: primary, cardinality: few, freshness: on_open}
actions:
  - {key: pay, importance: primary, intent: pay, what: pay the amount due, precondition: a way to pay is chosen and an amount is due, effect: [call OP-S030, external_flow payments, go SCR-015], errors: [network, forbidden, validation_failed, conflict], flags: [idempotent]}
states:   # what each must communicate, not how
  - {kind: "domain:conflict", message: "Something in the order changed, such as a price or availability; the user must agree to the change before paying."}
  - {kind: "domain:payment_declined", message: The payment was declined; no order is placed and another method can be tried.}
  - {kind: "domain:payment_pending", message: The payment result is not known yet; the user cannot pay again meanwhile.}
  - {kind: error, message: Something failed; say what happened in plain words and offer a retry.}
  - {kind: forbidden, message: The user's role may not see or do this; say so and where to go instead.}
  - {kind: loading, message: Nothing to show yet; the user must still see that content is coming.}
  - {kind: offline, message: "There is no network; show saved data, and say which actions are unavailable and why."}
  - {kind: success, message: What the user did worked; say what changed.}
copy_keys: [lib.checkout.domain.conflict, lib.checkout.domain.payment_declined, lib.checkout.domain.payment_pending, lib.common.error, lib.common.forbidden, lib.common.loading, lib.common.offline, lib.common.success, scr_014.amount_due_order_label, scr_014.amount_due_payment_label, scr_014.methods_payment_label, scr_014.pay, scr_014.title]
analytics: [payment_paid]
accessibility: the result of pay the amount due is announced to assistive technology
acceptance:
  - GIVEN the user has typical data and a working network WHEN the user uses Pay for order for its main purpose THEN the main purpose is achieved and the result is confirmed in plain words
  - GIVEN the user pays and the payment is declined WHEN the decline is received THEN the user is told the order was not paid for and why if known, no order is placed, and another payment method can be tried
  - GIVEN the result of what the user did is not known yet WHEN the user is on Pay for order THEN the user is told the result is pending and cannot repeat the action by mistake, and the final result appears here when known
  - GIVEN the device has no network while the user is on Pay for order WHEN the user opens Pay for order or acts on it THEN saved data is shown as possibly out of date, actions that need the network say so, and queued actions are sent when the network returns
  - GIVEN the user sends the same thing twice, by repeating it or by a slow connection WHEN the second request arrives THEN the thing is created once, and the user sees one clear result
  - GIVEN a signed-in buyer on Pay for order WHEN they pay the amount due THEN the change is saved and the person reaches SCR-015
  - GIVEN a signed-in buyer on Pay for order and the request fails with validation failed WHEN they pay the amount due THEN they stay here, see the reason in plain words and can try again or leave
mock: {profiles: [broken, typical], hero: ["ENT-006:payment_pending", "ENT-006:placed"]}
confirm: [RUL-S015 payments pending result]

